{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"REAL DEFECT FOUND BY CI AFTER THE RECHECK — A STACKING-ORDER ERROR, AND THE MOST INSTRUCTIVE ONE\nOF THE RUN.\nThe recheck was right: the environmental fault cleared and the job got past checkout, ran pytest on\nall four platforms, and failed identically on each with\n  ERROR tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py\n  ERROR tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity.py\n    Failed: 'allow_unharnessed_subprocess' not found in `markers` configuration option\n\nCAUSE: --strict-markers is on. The marker is REGISTERED in tests/conftest.py by 2506 (the guard),\nbut those two files USE it and both are owned by 2503 — BELOW 2506 in the stack. My tip was fine;\nevery intermediate patchset was not. Gerrit verifies each patchset independently, so a dependency\npointing UP the stack breaks the lower change while the branch tip stays green. My full-tier run had\ntested only the TIP and could never have caught it.\nOrigin of the mistake: the guard subagent correctly marked 19 test files, two of which belong to an\nearlier commit; when I split the worktree into per-commit amends I put those two files' markers into\n2503 along with the rest of their content, without asking which commit the MARKER depended on.\n\nFIX: stripped both decorators from 2503's versions and added them in 2506, so the commit that\nregisters the marker is also the one that first uses it. Verified the scope first — exactly two of\nthe nineteen marked files sit below 2506; the rest are at or above it.\n\nNEW CHECK, and the one I should have had from the start:\nscripts-style verify_each_patchset.sh checks out EVERY commit in the stack and runs\n'pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit' at each. Result:\n  ok b2b57ed86b03 2503 (14972)  ok 36489ad381a4 2504 (14972)  ok 8041c45daba2 2505 (14992)\n  ok c473a6bec516 2506 (15019)  ok 65d8c6dd322b 2507 (15019)  ok 1d4c6f18af58 ratchet (15047)\n  ALL PATCHSETS COLLECT CLEAN\nThe counts rising monotonically as each commit adds its own tests is itself the evidence that each\nstands alone.\nAlso verified the TIP is byte-identical to the tree that passed 14,997 tests — only the DISTRIBUTION\nof two decorators across commits changed — so the full-tier result still applies without re-running\n44 minutes of tests.\nPushed all six as patchset 3."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788332565070219001,"uuid":"605feed8-076d-4313-8fd7-5d2ad5b8ab83"}